From 3372cbbf5826e9aae9dcda8f083986059f8b3b19 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ObliviOS Build <build@oblivios.local>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 13:49:13 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/5] airpods: scope the Device ID vendor and L2CAP mode to
 registered peers and add BluetoothDevice#setAirPodsIdentity

airpods: scope Device-ID vendor and L2CAP mode to registered AirPods peers only

Adds a bonded-device-scoped identity mechanism (ADR-108, amending ADR-106
design section 6.2): a new privileged permission and AIDL method let
ObliviOS's own signed AirPods app register a bonded device it has
validated via its own protocol handshake, using the existing native
interop-database mechanism under a new INTEROP_AIRPODS_IDENTITY feature.
Native SDP and L2CAP code then consult this registration, following the
existing per-peer sdp_dynamic_change_hfp_version and l2c_should_skip_ertm
precedents, to scope the Device-ID vendor presentation and the L2CAP
channel-mode fallback to that one registered BD_ADDR only. Every other
peer's SDP query and every other Bluetooth connection is unaffected, and
the local Device-ID record BTA_DmSetLocalDiRecord sets is never touched.

airpods: add exact-match, bond-gated identity registry

airpods: register identity through a dedicated btif call and clear it on unbond

airpods: serve the SDP vendor override from a copy, gate hooks on registry and bond, drop the interop feature

airpods: add BluetoothDevice#setAirPodsIdentity for the AirPods app
